menu "CoffeeProbe fault tests"

    choice PROBE_FAULT_TEST
        prompt "Deliberate fault (test builds only)"
        default PROBE_FAULT_TEST_NONE
        help
            For the fault-injection session (#26): makes the probe fail on purpose once,
            30 s after power-on, to check that it restarts by itself and shows the reason on
            the Diagnostics screen and in the boot log. It does not fault again right after its
            own restart (so the reason can be read), only after a power-on or another restart. Never in committed defaults (guards.sh).
            Build one with: scripts/flash.sh --fault hang (or crash).

        config PROBE_FAULT_TEST_NONE
            bool "None (normal firmware)"

        config PROBE_FAULT_TEST_HANG
            bool "Freeze: the health task stops feeding the watchdog"
            help
                Expected: task watchdog panic about 5 s later, reboot, Diagnostics shows
                "Last reset: Freeze".

        config PROBE_FAULT_TEST_CRASH
            bool "Crash: the health task aborts"
            help
                Expected: panic, coredump, reboot, Diagnostics shows "Last reset: Crash" and
                "Crash record: Saved".
    endchoice

endmenu
